The tokenization mode: normal, or decompose with a Penalty . It is the counterpart of the Rust lindera::mode::Mode (see Segmenter ), and setMode() and the Tokenizer constructor take it: Normal mode -- standard dictionary-cost-based tokenization Decompose mode -- penalty-based decomposition of compound words Mode has no constructor, so new Mode() throws; the static factories below create a mode. A mode cannot be changed. Mode.normal() Creates normal mode. const { Mode } = require("lindera"); const mode = Mode.normal(); Mode.decompose(penalty?) Creates decompose mode with penalty, a Penalty object. null or undefined (the default) uses the default penalty, and a field left out keeps its default. A value that is not an object, or a field that is not an integer in its range, throws an InvalidArg error. const decompose = Mode.decompose(); // the default penalty
const custom = Mode.decompose({ kanjiPenaltyLengthPenalty: 0 }); Mode.fromStr(name) Creates a mode from its name, as the Rust Mode parses one: "normal" is normal mode, and "decompose" is decompose mode with the default penalty. The name is case sensitive; any other name, including "Normal" and "Decompose", throws an Error whose message contains Invalid mode. Use it for a mode name read at run time, such as a setting: const mode = Mode.fromStr("decompose");
console.log(mode.equals(Mode.decompose()));
// true Properties and Methods Member Type Description name string The name of the mode, "normal" or "decompose" (a read-only property) penalty Penalty | null The penalty of decompose mode, as a copy with every field set, or null for normal mode (a read-only property). Changing the copy does not change the mode isNormal() boolean Whether this is normal mode isDecompose() boolean Whether this is decompose mode equals(other) boolean Whether other has the same name and penalty. A value that is not a Mode throws an InvalidArg error toString() string The name of the mode, as name === compares objects, not modes: each call of Mode.normal() returns a new object, so compare modes with equals. const { Mode } = require("lindera"); const mode = Mode.decompose({ kanjiPenaltyLengthPenalty: 0 });
console.log(mode.name, mode.isNormal(), mode.isDecompose());
// decompose false true // A copy with every field set: the field left out has its default
const penalty = mode.penalty;
console.log(penalty.kanjiPenaltyLengthPenalty, penalty.otherPenaltyLengthPenalty);
// 0 1700 // Changing the copy does not change the mode
penalty.otherPenaltyLengthPenalty = 0;
console.log(mode.penalty.otherPenaltyLengthPenalty);
// 1700 console.log(Mode.normal().penalty);
// null console.log(Mode.decompose().equals(Mode.fromStr("decompose")));
// true
console.log(mode.equals(Mode.decompose()));
// false
console.log(`${Mode.normal()}`);
// normal

