A plain object (the TypeScript type Penalty) with the penalty parameters of decompose mode. Every field is optional, and a field left out keeps its default: Property Type Description kanjiPenaltyLengthThreshold number Length threshold for kanji sequences before a penalty is applied, an integer 0 or more (default: 2) kanjiPenaltyLengthPenalty number Penalty value for long kanji sequences, a 32-bit signed integer (default: 3000) otherPenaltyLengthThreshold number Length threshold for other character sequences before a penalty is applied, an integer 0 or more (default: 7) otherPenaltyLengthPenalty number Penalty value for long other-character sequences, a 32-bit signed integer (default: 1700) Pass it to Mode.decompose() , and the mode to setMode() or to the Tokenizer constructor . Without length penalties, decompose mode keeps long words whole, as normal mode does: const { Mode, Tokenizer, TokenizerBuilder, loadDictionary } = require("lindera"); const text = "関西国際空港限定トートバッグ";
