The tokenization mode: normal, or decompose with a Penalty . It is the counterpart of the Rust Mode (see Tokenization Modes ), and setMode() and the Tokenizer constructor take it. Mode has no public constructor: new Mode() is a TypeScript error, and in JavaScript it creates an object whose methods throw. Create a mode with a static method instead: Static method Description Mode.normal() Normal mode: standard tokenization based on dictionary cost Mode.decompose(penalty?) Decompose mode: compound words are decomposed using penalty-based segmentation. penalty is a Penalty ; null or undefined (the default) uses the default penalty. A value that is not a Penalty throws an error string (penalty must be a Penalty) Mode.fromStr(name) The mode named "normal" or "decompose" (with the default penalty). The name is case sensitive; any other name throws an error string that contains Invalid mode Property / Method Type Description name string "normal" or "decompose" (read-only) penalty Penalty or undefined A copy of the penalty of decompose mode, or undefined for normal mode (read-only) isNormal() boolean Whether this is normal mode isDecompose() boolean Whether this is decompose mode equals(other) boolean Whether other has the same name and penalty. A value that is not a Mode throws Error("expected instance of Mode") toString() string The name, as name returns it A Mode cannot be changed. Mode.decompose() keeps its own copy of the Penalty, and penalty returns another copy, so changing either Penalty afterwards does not change the mode. The Penalty passed to Mode.decompose() stays usable, and so does a Mode passed to setMode() or to the Tokenizer constructor. import { Mode, Penalty } from 'lindera-wasm-ipadic'; const mode = Mode.decompose(new Penalty(undefined, 0));
console.log(mode.name, mode.isNormal(), mode.isDecompose());
// decompose false true
console.log(`${mode}`, mode.penalty.kanji_penalty_length_penalty);
// decompose 0
console.log(mode.equals(Mode.decompose()), Mode.fromStr("decompose").equals(Mode.decompose()));
// false true
console.log(Mode.normal().penalty);
// undefined

