Error type for Lindera operations. const error = new LinderaError("message");
console.log(error.message); // "message"
console.log(error.toString()); // "message" Property / Method Type Description message string Error message toString() string Returns the error message [!NOTE] LinderaError is exported as a utility class, but the current error paths in TokenizerBuilder, Tokenizer, Mode, and the dictionary-loading functions (lindera-wasm/src/tokenizer.rs, lindera-wasm/src/mode.rs, lindera-wasm/src/dictionary.rs) all reject with JsValue::from_str(...), not a JsLinderaError/LinderaError instance. In practice, failures thrown by these APIs surface in JavaScript as plain strings. The exception is an argument that is not an instance of the class a method takes, such as a mode name passed to setMode(): the JS glue checks it before calling into Rust and throws an Error whose message is expected instance of <class> (here, expected instance of Mode). Catch them with catch (e) { ... } and treat e as a string or an Error, not as a LinderaError instance.

